WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:18.160
When Clara's father stepped onto the ground in front of Grandfather's hut, two girls walked toward him.

2
00:00:18.161 --> 00:00:27.033
Leaning on a smaller girl, whose eyes were dancing with joy, was a tall girl with fair hair and pink cheeks.

3
00:00:27.034 --> 00:00:32.774
She reminded Herr Sesemann of his late wife, and he almost thought he was dreaming.

4
00:00:32.775 --> 00:00:34.958
"Don't you know me, Papa?"

5
00:00:34.959 --> 00:00:39.010
called Clara, her face beaming with happiness.

6
00:00:39.011 --> 00:00:41.481
He stared at the two children.

7
00:00:41.482 --> 00:00:45.269
All at once, tears streamed from his eyes.

8
00:00:45.270 --> 00:00:49.519
He ran to Clara and clasped her in his arms.

9
00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.587
He stepped back to look at her again.

10
00:00:52.588 --> 00:00:54.572
"Are you my little Clara?

11
00:00:54.573 --> 00:00:59.992
Are you really my Clara?" he kept saying over and over.

12
00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:02.892
Heidi's heart beat with gladness.

13
00:01:02.893 --> 00:01:08.958
Herr Sesemann had always been good to her, and she was thrilled to see him so happy.

14
00:01:08.959 --> 00:01:16.562
Grandmamma introduced Herr Sesemann to Grandfather, and everyone settled down at Grandfather's table to talk.

15
00:01:16.563 --> 00:01:22.013
After a few moments, they heard a rustling noise from behind the goats' shed.

16
00:01:22.014 --> 00:01:26.933
"I think someone is hiding there," said Grandfather.

17
00:01:26.934 --> 00:01:29.923
Everyone looked; it was Peter.

18
00:01:29.924 --> 00:01:34.982
When Herr Sesemann saw Peter peek out from his hiding place, he called to him,

19
00:01:34.983 --> 00:01:38.120
"Come out, boy. Don't be afraid."

20
00:01:38.121 --> 00:01:40.873
Peter was scared stiff.

21
00:01:40.874 --> 00:01:47.524
He knew everyone was watching, so he screwed up his courage and came forward.

22
00:01:47.525 --> 00:01:54.483
"It was I. I broke it to pieces, and no one can put it together again," he exclaimed.

23
00:01:54.484 --> 00:01:58.894
Confused, Grandmamma and Herr Sesemann looked at each other.

24
00:01:58.895 --> 00:02:03.617
"Is that poor boy out of his mind?" asked Herr Sesemann.

25
00:02:03.618 --> 00:02:07.359
"Not in the least," said Grandfather.

26
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:16.624
"It turns out that he was the wind that sent Clara's wheelchair down the mountain, and he is expecting his well-deserved punishment."

27
00:02:16.625 --> 00:02:19.590
But nobody wanted to punish Peter.

28
00:02:19.591 --> 00:02:25.319
Grandmamma thought he looked like a nice boy who had acted recklessly.

29
00:02:25.320 --> 00:02:34.929
Peter explained everything to her, including how he had been jealous of Heidi for having so many visitors and how he had missed seeing her.

30
00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:40.474
"You are a good boy to tell us," said Grandmamma, with a smile.

31
00:02:40.475 --> 00:02:45.716
"Now I will give you a gift for being truthful."

32
00:02:45.717 --> 00:02:48.774
Peter could hardly believe his ears.

33
00:02:48.775 --> 00:02:53.334
After careful thought, he shyly asked for a penny.

34
00:02:53.335 --> 00:02:57.902
Grandmamma laughed, opening her purse.

35
00:02:57.903 --> 00:03:05.757
"I will give you enough pennies to have a penny a week for a whole year!" she declared.

36
00:03:05.758 --> 00:03:10.878
After watching this scene, Herr Sesemann put his hand on Clara's shoulder.

37
00:03:10.879 --> 00:03:16.397
"Grandfather," he said, "you have given me a gift that can never be repaid.

38
00:03:16.398 --> 00:03:22.533
But if there is any way I can thank you, please let me know."

39
00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:25.556
Grandfather was quiet for a moment.

40
00:03:25.557 --> 00:03:33.347
"I am poor and old," he said, "and I have nothing to leave to Heidi when I die.

41
00:03:33.348 --> 00:03:44.201
If you promise me that Heidi will never have to leave the mountain and earn her living among strangers, then you will be rewarding me richly."

42
00:03:44.202 --> 00:03:46.955
Clara's father did not hesitate.

43
00:03:46.956 --> 00:03:50.992
He said, "I consider Heidi as one of my family.

44
00:03:50.993 --> 00:03:53.108
She will always be looked after.

45
00:03:53.109 --> 00:03:55.170
I promise you that."

46
00:03:55.171 --> 00:04:02.267
Then, Grandmamma realized that Heidi should be rewarded as well for being such a good friend to Clara.

47
00:04:02.268 --> 00:04:08.438
"Heidi, what would you like for your reward?"

48
00:04:08.439 --> 00:04:14.938
Heidi replied immediately, "I would like a warm, beautiful bed for Grannie.

49
00:04:14.939 --> 00:04:17.506
Nothing would please me more!"

50
00:04:17.507 --> 00:04:21.666
Grandmamma happily agreed.

51
00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:29.822
Just then, the sun began to set, and its warm glow shone on the mountaintops in beautiful shades of red and orange.

52
00:04:29.823 --> 00:04:33.411
Heidi felt that her life was truly blessed.

53
00:04:33.412 --> 00:04:42.808
All her friends and family were happy and healthy, and she would never have to leave the mountain again.

54
00:04:42.809 --> 00:05:37.042
[caption_out@
